                "type": "text",
                "content": "Sometimes a number is hidden behind a letter or a box. Algebra is just the clever art of working out what that missing number must be.",
                "cognition": "knowing"
            },
            {
                "type": "key",
                "content": "A letter stands for an unknown number. To find it, undo what was done — do the opposite operation.",
                "cognition": "knowing"
            },
            {
                "type": "example",
                "content": "Solving n + 5 = 12.",
                "steps": [
                    "Something plus 5 makes 12.",
                    "Undo the +5 by subtracting: 12 - 5 = 7.",
                    "So n = 7. Check: 7 + 5 = 12. Correct!"
                ],
                "cognition": "knowing"
            },
            {
                "type": "fillblank",
